1479	    // idles (NCU large4k: barrier 31%, tensor 57% vs FA3 70%). Serializing the wgmma-ISSUE phase via two
1480	    // named barriers (8/9, cnt=256) staggers them by one step: while WG_a feeds the tensor core, WG_b runs
1481	    // softmax, and vice-versa. The token stays balanced across work items -- both WGs run the same n_cnt
1482	    // (same work index), so each does exactly one sync+arrive per inner-loop step. Gate: CM==128 (2
1483	    // consumer WGs) && HD==128. Big heads (192/256) are already tensor-pipe-saturated per tile so
1484	    // serializing the issue only adds barrier latency (-0.02 hd192/hd256). On the PERSIST path hd64
